# KhayaOS Implementation Standard (Mandatory)

Before any code change, read `docs/IMPLEMENTATION_STANDARD.md`.

## Non-negotiable rules

1. **Extend, don't replace** — reuse existing services, controllers, RBAC, feature flags, migrations, and UI components. No parallel implementations.
2. **Complete production work only** — no TODOs, placeholders, scaffolds, or UI-only features. Backend must enforce limits and permissions.
3. **Architecture** — Laravel modular monolith; business logic in services (`Controller → Service → Repository`); module communication via events; tenant isolation on every query.
4. **Stack** — Laravel + Next.js PWA + PostgreSQL + Sanctum. Additive API changes only.
5. **Backend deliverables** — migrations, services, thin controllers, audit logs on mutations, PHPUnit feature tests.
6. **Frontend deliverables** — types in `lib/types.ts`, API in `services/`, KhayaOS UI (Card, Button, Anek font), `npm run build` must pass.
7. **QA gate** — `php artisan test` and `npm run build` pass before considering work done.
8. **Deploy** — see `docs/VPS_DEPLOY.md`. On VPS, **every git command must use** `-c safe.directory=/www/wwwroot/khayaos.prohost.cloud`. When the user asks for a VPS deploy snippet, use the full block in that doc (pull + log + migrate + PricingSeeder + build + pm2 restart).

Reference implementation: Phase 1.0.2 SaaS Commercialization (`ffa9d2f`). Follow the same depth and completeness for all future features.

## VPS deploy snippet (mandatory format)

When providing production deploy commands, **always** include the safe.directory prefix on git commands. Never output bare `git pull` for this server.

```bash
cd /www/wwwroot/khayaos.prohost.cloud
git -c safe.directory=/www/wwwroot/khayaos.prohost.cloud pull origin main
git -c safe.directory=/www/wwwroot/khayaos.prohost.cloud log -1 --oneline
cd backend && /www/server/php/83/bin/php artisan migrate --force
/www/server/php/83/bin/php artisan db:seed --class=PricingSeeder --force
cd ../frontend && npm run build
pm2 restart khayaos-frontend khayaos-queue khayaos-reverb
```
